# ID: GCI-SPL-WIN-002
# Title: Registry Run and RunOnce persistence changes
# Platform: Splunk Enterprise / Splunk Enterprise Security
# Type: Endpoint threat-hunting query
# Data source: Sysmon Event ID 13 (Registry Value Set)
# Required fields: index, sourcetype, EventCode, TargetObject, Details, Image, User, Computer
# Maturity: Draft
# Assumptions: Sysmon Event ID 13 is collected; TargetObject and Details are extracted from XML.
# False positives: Legitimate installers, updaters, endpoint agents and approved logon scripts.
# Tuning: Baseline software deployment windows and signed installer processes; investigate unusual paths, user-writable directories and unexpected parent processes.
# ATT&CK: T1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder.
# Validation: Not run against a Splunk instance. Verify exact registry field extraction first.

index=windows sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=13
| where like(lower(TargetObject), "%\\software\\microsoft\\windows\\currentversion\\run%")
    OR like(lower(TargetObject), "%\\software\\microsoft\\windows\\currentversion\\runonce%")
| table _time Computer User Image TargetObject Details
| sort - _time
